Hello,

The rtnetlink module of Linux kernel has ab information leak vulnerability
In the file "net/core/rtnetlink.c", The stack object =E2=80=9Cmap=E2=80=9D =
has a total size
of
32 bytes. Its last 4 bytes are padding generated by compiler. These padding
bytes are not initialized and sent out via =E2=80=9Cnla_put=E2=80=9D.


Fix info:
*http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-netdev&m=3D146230822606494&w=3D2
<http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-netdev&m=3D146230822606494&w=3D2>*
*http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-netdev&m=3D146239324530095&w=3D2
<http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-netdev&m=3D146239324530095&w=3D2>*

Please help assign a CVE to this vulnerability.



